      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I currently have a second account on a separate computer which sits idle in a public pug. It's been going strong for the last few days and every 12-24 hours i'll create a new instance. This appears to fix the issue for most people as it will only happen to the master. \nHowever if 10+ people join all at once there is a small chance the glitch may happen to one of the people that recently joined and not the master. \nWhat's interesting is that person will have like a 'sync'd' version of the chair glitch. They seem to always be sitting in the same chair on everyones screen. I notice this tends to happen with the instance starter too pretty often.\nI've also posted this on reddit for more exposure as not all users can post in the canny: https://www.reddit.com/r/VRchat/comments/lno8hh/the_infamous_chair_glitch/\nI don't think the team realizes how frustrating this specific bug is. People can be having a fantastic time and then conversation always turns to this bug. It's extremely annoying and makes people just give up and quit.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
